{"type":"standard","title":"Ati language (Philippines)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ati language (Philippines)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3217458","titles":{"canonical":"Ati_language_(Philippines)","normalized":"Ati language (Philippines)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ati language (Philippines)</span></span>"},"pageid":47862242,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1292700529","tid":"ba540540-3bab-11f0-8615-7d0649f83cf4","timestamp":"2025-05-28T10:08:40Z","description":"Austronesian language spoken in Philippines","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ati_language_(Philippines)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ati_language_(Philippines)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ati_language_(Philippines)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ati_language_(Philippines)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ati_language_(Philippines)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ati_language_(Philippines)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ati_language_(Philippines)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ati_language_(Philippines)"}},"extract":"Ati (Inati), or Binisaya nga Inati, is an Austronesian language of the island of Panay in the Philippines. The variety spoken in northern Panay is also called Sogodnin. The Ati people also speak Kinaray-a and Hiligaynon.","extract_html":"<p><b>Ati</b> (<i>Inati</i>), or <b>Binisaya nga Inati</b>, is an Austronesian language of the island of Panay in the Philippines. The variety spoken in northern Panay is also called <b>Sogodnin</b>. The Ati people also speak Kinaray-a and Hiligaynon.</p>"}